# paperclip fleet read

Use this skill when Zay asks what exists in Paperclip or asks for a cross-company
fleet snapshot.

## scope
- companies list and company detail
- company members and billing state
- cross-company metadata
- active, paused, and errored company state

## protocol
1. Start from live Paperclip state. Do not answer from memory alone.
2. Prefer the operator credential. If running in company-key pivot mode, name
   the company explicitly before each company-scoped read.
3. Summarize by company slug or id. Keep client-sensitive details out of
   cross-company pattern notes.

## commands
```sh
python /home/agent/.hermes/envoy/paperclip_operator.py list-companies
python /home/agent/.hermes/envoy/paperclip_operator.py api GET /companies
python /home/agent/.hermes/envoy/paperclip_operator.py api GET /companies/<company_id> --company-id <company_id>
python /home/agent/.hermes/envoy/paperclip_operator.py api GET /companies/<company_id>/members --company-id <company_id>
python /home/agent/.hermes/envoy/paperclip_operator.py api GET /companies/<company_id>/billing --company-id <company_id>
```

## output
Use lowercase headers. Include the evidence source and timestamp when practical.
